      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(a+3)^2-4(a)(1)\\\\\\Delta&=a^2+2a+9\\\\\\Delta&=(a+1)^2+8.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $(a+1)^2\\ge0$, we have $\\Delta\\ge8>0$. Also, $a\\ne0$, so the equation is quadratic. Hence it has two distinct real roots for every $a\\ne0$.",
